+# Verification protocol and research acceptance — vNext.3 + PG-SMA
+
+## Structural acceptance
+
+| Gate | Test | Hard pass |
+|---|---|---|
+| 0.1 | Native disabled-semantic identity | Same raw box/obj/class outputs for same model/weights |
+| 0.2 | Native/semantic optimizer isolation | Identical native parameter update, BN buffers, optimizer momentum, assignments, and native EMA with/without semantic update |
+| 0.3 | Predictor activation | Nonzero candidate/teacher gradient to zero-init terminal; downstream hidden/gate gradients on subsequent steps |
+| 0.4 | Prototype scores | Permutation-invariant within class, finite normalized vectors, meaningful K=1/BG BCE |
+| 0.5 | Alignment and gate | Identity correction zero, |delta logit| <= budget, no test-time state change, per-image batch independence |
+| 0.6 | SCPA | Maximum cardinality on enumerated graph, one GT per anchor, protected core, no out-of-envelope forced match, explicit budget/ineligible reporting |
+| 0.7 | Data | No dropped labels after mosaic/transform/collate, crowd/ignore safety, correct GT pixel-size stratification, valid padding masks |
+| 0.8 | Dynamic inputs | Supported stride-aligned H/W; no grid-cache stale shape, no Python shape specialization in export graph |
+| 0.9 | AMP and resume | Independent native/semantic skip logic; teacher EMA after successful semantic steps; consistent raw/EMA checkpoints |
+
+## Experimental falsification (do not infer from unit tests)
+
+| Component | Compare against | Evidence required |
+|---|---|---|
+| SCPA | Native SimOTA under fixed loss | GT coverage and actual micro/medium/macro detection improve; training cost acceptable |
+| Per-GT loss reduction | SCPA + native loss reduction | More balanced size-gradient attribution and AP/AR, no noisy-micro overfitting |
+| SPI | Same native model with zero-gate | Extra micro evidence without sacrificing medium/large localization; memory/latency justified |
+| Tribrid global/context | Same model with branch off | Useful conditional context without masked small-object feature loss |
+| Prototypes | Native-only | Hard-negative/class discrimination and clean/shift AP, including K=1 |
+| Local prediction | Center-only and spatially shuffled neighbors | True context improves detection-grounded corrections |
+| JEPA auxiliary | No consistency loss | Better held-out perturbation/adverse detection, not merely lower cosine loss |
+| PG-SMA | Separately trained memory-only calibration | Improved class ranking with no scale-specific harms |
+| Gate | Ungated candidate | Helpful acceptance and harmful rejection; no perpetual shutoff |
+| Direct vs retraction | Same source-trained semantic foundation | Better AP/AR/false-positive and edge cost; not assumed by geometry |
+| IoU loss | Native YOLOX IoU | AP75, box geometry and micro/medium/macro gradient scaling |
+
+## Clean-only protocol
+
+Training gradients from clean labeled source and source-derived semantic perturbations only. Clean validation and held-out source perturbation families for iteration. Unseen adverse datasets (ACDC, DAWN, ExDark, BDD adverse) and UAV scenarios kept separate by taxonomy; use genuinely fresh evaluation for final claims. Previously inspected ACDC subsets are diagnostics, not unbiased hyperparameter-selection sets.
+
+## Nine-criterion scoring
+
+- AP50:95; AP50; AP75; AR100; AP/AR-small, medium and large.
+- Additional **input-pixel** micro bins and continuous AP/AR versus target width/area (COCO small alone is too coarse for UAV).
+- Native-only and corrected predictions at *every checkpoint*; per-scale positive count and unmatched GT reasons; pre-NMS candidate recall, post-NMS recall, score-versus-IoU correlation and false-positive counts.
+- Track 80-epoch trajectories, checkpoint/EMA/optimizer drift, gate acceptance, correction magnitude by level, prototype mode occupancy, class confusion and teacher representation drift.
+- Pre-register meaningful non-inferiority margins using paired intervals and multiple seeds. A 0.001 AP difference is not automatically evidence.
+- Target hardware: ONNX checker, ONNX-runtime parity, TensorRT compilation/profile/parity, P50/P95 latency, peak VRAM and full preprocess/inference/NMS timing. Runtime 4K cannot be guaranteed from FLOPs.
+
+**Hard rule:** A component failing to demonstrate task benefit against the correct ablation is not part of the final vNext.3 detector. Structural correctness, all-scale performance and transfer are separate gates; no component may inherit a claim from another's test result.
